{"pull": {"id": "number:21973", "number": 21973, "title": "KAFKA-20398: Fix memory leak by removing StreamsThreadMetricsDelegatingReporter from metrics registry on thread shutdown", "state": "closed", "draft": false, "created_at": "2026-04-06T19:25:04Z", "closed_at": "2026-04-07T19:00:07Z", "merged_at": "2026-04-07T19:00:07Z", "user": {"login": "sstremler", "id": 5159983, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjUxNTk5ODM=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5159983?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler", "html_url": "https://github.com/sstremler", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/sstremler/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "When a stream thread in Kafka Streams crashes,\n`StreamsUncaughtExceptionHandler` can be configured to replace the\ncrashed thread with a new one. Each time a new stream thread is created,\nit adds a new `StreamsThreadMetricsDelegatingReporter` to it. However,\nwhen the old thread shuts down, its reporter is never removed from the\nregistry implying \"unbounded\" memory growth.\n\nThis bug was introduced via https://github.com/apache/kafka/pull/17021\n\nThis PR ensures that the existing\n`StreamsThreadMetricsDelegatingReporter` is removed when a thread is\nshutting down.\n\nReviewers: Matthias J. Sax <matthias@confluent.io>, Bill Bejeck\n <bbejeck@apache.org>\n", 